From: StellarSeal <emnoigi1452@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:33:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 091/120] Remove per-node allocations from World light
 propagation

World.c (the sky/block light BFS) allocated a BlockPosition per dequeued node plus six more for the neighbor probes, cloned EnumDirection.values() per node, and every probe did isLoaded + chunk lookup + BlockPosition clamp. Now:
- new World.getBrightness(EnumSkyBlock, int x, int y, int z) and Chunk.getBrightness(EnumSkyBlock, int, int, int) give the same result as the BlockPosition variants (y clamp, isValidLocation, unloaded-chunk default, height-map light for empty sections), with one chunk lookup; the allow-permanent-chunk-loaders side effect (Chunk.d = false) is preserved.
- c() reads neighbors by coordinates, reuses one MutableBlockPosition for the read-only per-node work, and only allocates a BlockPosition when a node is actually written (setter semantics unchanged).
- the private target-light computation uses ints and a cached direction array instead of a pooled position and values().
Queue encoding, the radius-17 cutoff, the overflow guard and the write order are untouched, so output is bit-identical.

Tests: LightPropagationParityTest runs a verbatim copy of the old World.c/World.a on an identical world against the new code over 6 seeds x 400 random block changes (stone, torch, glowstone, leaves, water, air; floor with pillars; sky light above the height map), a 12x12x12 paste/relight/removal cycle, world-edge positions and a 20k-position getBrightness equivalence sweep (extremes, y<0, y>255, unloaded chunks, empty sections), comparing every sky and block nibble in all 16 sections of 16 chunks. LightPropagationPerfTest (same edits on fresh identical worlds, nibbles re-verified): glowstone cube paste 43 ms -> 31 ms (1.4x, 14x less allocation), torch place/remove 37 -> 20 ms (1.9x, 13.5x), mixed random edits 305 -> 208 ms (1.5x, 13.5x). Not covered: Chunk.n() still clones EnumDirection.values(); the real-world heightMap/skylight maintenance in Chunk.a is untouched and not exercised by the stub world.

